{"acceptance_length": 7.212765957446808, "acceptance_lengths": [5, 8, 3, 8, 9, 16, 6, 10, 4, 3, 1, 3, 1, 7, 12, 13, 3, 13, 5, 3, 2, 10, 7, 13, 13, 4, 4, 3, 2, 5, 2, 3, 4, 10, 8, 3, 8, 11, 6, 9, 16, 16, 5, 16, 9, 7, 10], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23421988352, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23421970944, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given the following information:\n\n- **Twenty dozen cups** cost **$1200 less** than the total cost of **half a dozen plates** sold at **$6000 each**.\n- We are to find the **total cost of buying each cup**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the quantities\n\n- **Twenty dozen cups** = $ 20 \\times 12 = 240 $ cups\n- **Half a dozen plates** = $ \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 = 3 $ plates\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the total cost of the plates\n\nEach plate costs **$6000**, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost of plates} = 3 \\times 6000 = 18000\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Set up the equation\n\nLet the **cost of one cup** be $ x $ dollars.\n\nThen, the **total cost of 240 cups** is:\n\n$$\n240x\n$$\n\nAccording to the problem:\n\n$$\n240x = 18000 - 1200\n$$\n\n$$\n240x = 16800\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Solve for $ x $\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{16800}{240} = 70\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{70}\n$$\n\nSo, the **total cost of buying each cup** is **$70**.", "decode_seconds": 1.6984300068579614, "draft_calls": 47, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 64, "method": "native_target_dflash", "output_hash": "6ab3bc4a878524abcde41a8b2ac3adaed8548aaca3b9a4da84d466842840e743", "output_tokens": 338, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23519278080, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23873978368, "problem_id": "gsm8k/5d6ed708fe454661", "profile_regions_ms": {"unattributed_runtime": 1736.5040928125381}, "rank": 0, "reference_answer": "145", "repetition": 0, "request_seconds": 1.7365040928125381, "reserved_memory_after_bytes": 23873978368, "reserved_memory_before_bytes": 23873978368, "target_calls": 47, "time_to_first_token_seconds": 0.030699