{"acceptance_length": 6.589285714285714, "acceptance_lengths": [9, 5, 4, 3, 13, 4, 8, 7, 1, 6, 3, 10, 7, 1, 2, 2, 5, 14, 4, 4, 6, 10, 7, 16, 2, 1, 3, 16, 4, 4, 1, 1, 8, 12, 16, 7, 7, 3, 2, 16, 5, 3, 2, 1, 13, 4, 8, 16, 1, 6, 16, 11, 4, 2, 10, 13], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23421988864, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23421971456, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given the following information:\n\n- On a certain day, the total cost of filling **20 helium balloons** was **$900**.\n- Two days later, the **cost of filling each balloon was increased by $20**.\n- Bentley went to fill **170 balloons** **after the price increase**.\n- We are to find how much **Bentley paid** for filling 170 balloons after the price increase.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the original cost per balloon\n\nWe are told that 20 balloons cost $900.\n\n$$\n\\text{Original cost per balloon} = \\frac{900}{20} = 45\n$$\n\nSo, the original price per balloon was **$45**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the new cost per balloon after the increase\n\nThe cost of filling each balloon was increased by **$20**.\n\n$$\n\\text{New cost per balloon} = 45 + 20 = 65\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the total cost for 170 balloons at the new price\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost} = 170 \\times 65\n$$\n\nLet\u2019s compute that:\n\n$$\n170 \\times 65 = (100 \\times 65) + (70 \\times 65) = 6500 + 4550 = 11050\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{11050}\n$$\n\nSo, **Bentley paid $11,050** to fill 170 balloons after the price increase.", "decode_seconds": 2.025892075151205, "draft_calls": 56, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 89, "method": "native_target_dflash", "output_hash": "d88f1b6919dd06f015142a0991805859da5f653fb285b1d4bf906fb81c5b22e0", "output_tokens": 368, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23528013824, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23915921408, "problem_id": "gsm8k/4e6419841f3b7e3a", "profile_regions_ms": {"unattributed_runtime": 2065.4678670689464}, "rank": 0, "reference_answer